  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Open Counter",
    "overview": "(The name was derived from the direction thesis, \"the desk is open: a calm white counter where the conversation itself is the hero\". The user did not choose a name.)\n\nThe system is a white counter with a conversation laid out on it. The page ground is white paper, type is near-black ink, and product moments sit on soft grey stages with big rounded corners. White chat cards float on those stages under quiet ambient shadows. One bright teal is the only colour, and it marks the actions and confirmations a visitor should notice: the primary pill, a booked date, a \"replies instantly\" dot. The inspiration, chosen by the user, is chatbot.com's approach: a friendly geometric sans, rounded shapes everywhere, and a mostly black, white and grey palette with one bright accent.\n\nThe feel is warm and approachable without being cute. Figtree carries everything. Display type is set heavy (800) and tight, so headlines feel confident while the round letterforms keep them friendly. Density is relaxed: generous section padding, short line lengths, and a lot of white around each stage so the chat stays the subject. Ink is used in two ways. It is the colour of text, and it fills full panels at the moments of commitment: the contact close and the featured plan.\n\nDepth is gentle. Flat grey stages hold white cards that lift slightly off them. Nothing is glossy, gradient-filled or loud; the teal and the conversation do the work.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "White paper ground, near-black ink text, soft grey stages: mono plus one accent.",
      "One bright teal accent; teal fills always carry ink text.",
      "Figtree only; 800-weight display with negative tracking; sentence case throughout.",
